  "tested": false,
  "verification": "V16 relocates shared runtime state to D801-D804 for the four pinned images in post-startup application use. All 45 changed source units and their baselines reproduce with the C166 assembler; exact descriptor payload matching proves 215 operand substitutions with instruction lengths, hooks, calibrations, defaults and other bytes retained. Offline exact installed-byte verification passes 240 native RAM coexistence cases and 16 retired-revision collision controls, together with feature, timing, boot/reset, diagnostic recovery and configured migration checks. This establishes bounded emulator behavior; bench and on-car validation remain required.",
  "title": "Ignition Cut",
  "user_description": "Independent ignition-cut limiter with RPM hysteresis, optional fixed injector pulse width and an optional fixed ignition angle in a configurable RPM region below the cut limit. Provides shared timing and combustion-observation recovery for Launch Control V16.",
  "description": "MS41.0 Ignition Cut V16 relocates its shared runtime state away from the native roughness/reference arrays: D801 is the request/marker byte, D802 is freshness, D803 is qualified timing observation, and D804 is timing source. All limiter, timing, diagnostic-guard and recovery behavior from ignition_cut_v15_ms410 is retained. Launch Control V16 uses this same owner. Cave geometry, calibration addresses, RPM bands, hysteresis, protection priority and erased-range defaults are unchanged. Exact compatible predecessor pairs migrate together and retain tuned calibration bytes.",
